TEXT.update({
    "The Vladimir Icon and all images of the Tenderness type": "Ikoni ya Vladimir na sura zote za namna ya Upole",
    "The Vladimir Icon of the Mother of God": "Ikoni ya Vladimir ya Mzazi-Mungu",
    "The Vladimir Icon of the Mother of God borne in procession, the Tatar host turning back from Moscow, the city delivered by the protection of the Theotokos without the drawing of a sword.": "Ikoni ya Vladimir ya Mzazi-Mungu ikibebwa katika maandamano, jeshi la Watatari likirudi nyuma kutoka Moscow, mji ukiokolewa kwa ulinzi wa Mzazi-Mungu bila upanga kufutwa.",
    "The Vladimir Icon of the Mother of God, of which it is a wonderworking copy": "Ikoni ya Vladimir ya Mzazi-Mungu, ambayo hii ni nakala yake itendayo miujiza",
    "The Vladimir Icon of the Mother of God, which Saint Andrew was carrying (May 21)": "Ikoni ya Vladimir ya Mzazi-Mungu, ambayo Mtakatifu Andrea alikuwa akiibeba (Mei 21)",
    "The Vladimir Icon's other feasts of deliverance (August 26 and June 23)": "Sikukuu nyingine za ukombozi za Ikoni ya Vladimir (Agosti 26 na Juni 23)",
    "The Vladimir Icon, of whose Tenderness type it is": "Ikoni ya Vladimir, ambayo ni ya namna yake ya Upole",
    "The Vladimir image of the Mother of God in its Volokolamsk copy, received in procession at the gates of Joseph's monastery, wonders flowing at its new home.": "Sura ya Vladimir ya Mzazi-Mungu katika nakala yake ya Volokolamsk, iliyopokelewa katika maandamano malangoni pa monasteri ya Iosifu, miujiza ikitiririka katika makao yake mapya.",
    "The Vyshgorod and other wonderworking icons of the Kyivan land": "Ikoni za Vyshgorod na nyingine zitendazo miujiza za nchi ya Kyiv",
    "The Wonderful Mountain, near Antioch": "Mlima wa Ajabu, karibu na Antiokia",
    "The Yaroslavl (Tenderness) and Yaroslavl-Kazan Icons": "Ikoni za Yaroslavl (Upole) na za Yaroslavl-Kazan",
    "The abbot of the Caves honored under his Far Caves title, one father answering to every style of his name.": "Abate wa Mapango anayeheshimiwa chini ya jina lake la Mapango ya Mbali, baba mmoja akijibu kwa kila namna ya jina lake.",
    "The aged apostle dictating his Gospel to Prochorus in the cave, or with the eagle, finger to his lips.": "Mtume mzee akimwagizia Prokoro Injili yake katika pango, au akiwa na tai, kidole midomoni pake.",
    "The aged first bishop of the imperial city vested at the altar, too old to attend the Council of Nicaea, sending his vicar Alexander and naming him his successor.": "Askofu wa kwanza mzee wa mji wa kifalme amevaa mavazi ya ibada madhabahuni, akiwa mzee mno kuhudhuria Mtaguso wa Nicea, akimtuma msaidizi wake Aleksandro na kumtaja kuwa mrithi wake.",
    "The aged youth of Scetis with a cherub guiding his hand over the desert, the skull of the pagan priest speaking at his feet, the staff of Anthony in his grasp.": "Kijana mzee wa Sketi akiwa na kerubi akiuongoza mkono wake juu ya jangwa, fuvu la kuhani wa kipagani likisema miguuni pake, fimbo ya Antonio mkononi mwake.",
    "The angel rousing Peter in Herod's prison, the chains falling from his wrists, the same chains enshrined and venerated by the faithful.": "Malaika akimwamsha Petro katika gereza la Herode, minyororo ikianguka kutoka mikononi mwake, minyororo ileile ikiwekwa na kuheshimiwa na waamini.",
    "The apostle bound upon the X-shaped cross, preaching to the people of Patras from his crucifixion.": "Mtume amefungwa juu ya msalaba wenye umbo la X, akiwahubiria watu wa Patra kutoka msalabani.",
    "The apostle to the Gentiles struck down by the light on the Damascus road, the sword of his martyrdom and the scroll of his epistles in his hands, the chief of the apostles with Peter.": "Mtume wa mataifa aliyeangushwa na nuru katika njia ya Damasko, upanga wa kuuawa kwake na gombo la nyaraka zake mikononi mwake, mkuu wa mitume pamoja na Petro.",
    "The apostle touching the wounded side of the risen Christ, or holding a builder's square before an Indian king.": "Mtume akigusa ubavu uliojeruhiwa wa Kristo aliyefufuka, au akishika pembe ya mjenzi mbele ya mfalme wa India.",
    "The apostolic enlighteners and first martyrs of Gaul": "Waangazaji wa kitume na mashahidi wa kwanza wa Gali",
    "The assembled fathers of the council holding icons of Christ and the Theotokos, the empress and patriarch presiding.": "Mababa wa mtaguso waliokusanyika wakishika ikoni za Kristo na za Mzazi-Mungu, malkia na patriaki wakiongoza.",
    "The bodies of the twelve lay unburied four days, untouched by beast or bird, and were then buried by the Christians": "Miili ya wale kumi na wawili ilikaa bila kuzikwa siku nne, bila kuguswa na mnyama wala ndege, kisha ikazikwa na Wakristo",
    "The brethren of the Svir monastery opening the founder's grave to find him incorrupt as one sleeping, the church rising above him receiving its true foundation.": "Ndugu wa monasteri ya Svir wakifungua kaburi la mwanzilishi na kumkuta hajaoza kama aliyelala, kanisa likiinuka juu yake likipokea msingi wake wa kweli.",
    "The brethren of the iron-bog monastery gathered at their founder's opened shrine, the second memory of James kept beside the first.": "Ndugu wa monasteri ya matope ya chuma wamekusanyika kwenye sanduku takatifu lililofunguliwa la mwanzilishi wao, kumbukumbu ya pili ya Yakobo ikihifadhiwa kando ya ya kwanza.",
    "The cave of Bethlehem still radiant, the Protomartyr's crown laid beside the manger, the feast continuing in glory.": "Pango la Bethlehemu likiwa bado linang'aa, taji ya Shahidi wa Kwanza ikiwekwa kando ya hori, sikukuu ikiendelea katika utukufu.",
    "The cave of Bethlehem still shining, the Church singing on through the days, the Sun of Righteousness rising over the lengthening light.": "Pango la Bethlehemu likiwa bado linang'aa, Kanisa likiimba katika siku zote, Jua la Haki likichomoza juu ya nuru inayoongezeka.",
    "The cave prepared and the manger swept, the Virgin arrived at Bethlehem, the first star awaited in the winter sky.": "Pango likiandaliwa na hori kufagiliwa, Bikira amewasili Bethlehemu, nyota ya kwanza ikingojwa katika anga la baridi.",
    "The cell-attendant of Sergius fallen on his face in the unbearable light, the Mother of God with the apostles filling the little cell, the meekest of the disciples granted the greatest of the sights.": "Mhudumu wa chumba wa Sergio akianguka kifudifudi katika nuru isiyovumilika, Mzazi-Mungu pamoja na mitume wakijaza chumba kidogo, mpole kuliko wanafunzi wote akipewa kuona kubwa kuliko yote.",
    "The centurion at the Cross as the Georgian tradition depicts him, spear in hand, confessing the Son of God.": "Akida msalabani kama mapokeo ya Georgia yamwonyeshavyo, mkuki mkononi, akimkiri Mwana wa Mungu.",
    "The chief man of Malta receiving the shipwrecked Apostle Paul, his father healed by the Apostle's hands, the same man vested at last as bishop of Athens with the martyr's crown descending.": "Mkuu wa Malta akimpokea Mtume Paulo aliyevunjikiwa na meli, babaye akiponywa kwa mikono ya Mtume, mtu yuleyule mwishowe akivikwa mavazi ya askofu wa Athene na taji ya shahidi ikishuka.",
    "The child Mary enthroned upon the third step of the sanctuary, the Church lingering in the light of her Entry.": "Mtoto Maria ameketi juu ya kipandio cha tatu cha patakatifu, Kanisa likikaa katika nuru ya Kuingia kwake.",
    "The child Mary led toward the Temple steps, the virgins with lamps preparing her way.": "Mtoto Maria akiongozwa kuelekea vipandio vya Hekalu, mabikira wenye taa wakiitayarisha njia yake.",
    "The child Mary within the sanctuary, the Church singing the festal hymns a final time.": "Mtoto Maria ndani ya patakatifu, Kanisa likiimba nyimbo za sikukuu kwa mara ya mwisho.",
    "The child-martyrs and their companions of the age of the emperors": "Watoto mashahidi na wenzao wa zama za wafalme",
    "The child-martyrs and virgin-martyrs of the age of the emperors": "Watoto mashahidi na mabikira mashahidi wa zama za wafalme",
    "The church of Pergamum of the Apocalypse": "Kanisa la Pergamo la Ufunuo",
    "The city of Constantinople shaken, walls and towers falling, the people in procession with litanies.": "Mji wa Konstantinopoli ukitikiswa, kuta na minara zikianguka, watu wakiwa katika maandamano na maombi.",
    "The clergy bearing the Cross in procession and blessing the waters, the faithful venerating.": "Makasisi wakibeba Msalaba katika maandamano na kubariki maji, waamini wakiheshimu.",
    "The companions of the God-bearer gathering the remains the lions left, the road from the Colosseum to Antioch, the city receiving its bishop home.": "Wenzake wa Mbeba-Mungu wakikusanya mabaki ambayo simba waliyaacha, njia kutoka Kolosseo hadi Antiokia, mji ukimpokea askofu wake nyumbani.",
    "The company of the Celtic saints of Britain": "Kundi la watakatifu wa Kikelti wa Britania",
})

TEXT.update({
    "The company of the New Martyrs under the Turkish yoke": "Kundi la Mashahidi Wapya chini ya nira ya Kituruki",
    "The company of the martyrs and ascetics of the Holy Mountain": "Kundi la mashahidi na watawa wa Mlima Mtakatifu",
    "The company of the monastic saints of Ireland": "Kundi la watakatifu wa kitawa wa Ireland",
    "The company of the twelve Minor Prophets": "Kundi la manabii wadogo kumi na wawili",
    "The confessors and martyrs of the First Iconoclasm": "Wakiri na mashahidi wa Upinzani wa Kwanza wa Ikoni",
    "The confessors and martyrs of the iconoclast persecutions": "Wakiri na mashahidi wa mateso ya wapinga-ikoni",
    "The confessors of Orthodoxy against the Union of Brest": "Wakiri wa Othodoksi dhidi ya Muungano wa Brest",
    "The confessors of the Diocletian persecution and of Julian the Apostate": "Wakiri wa mateso ya Diokletiano na ya Yuliano Mwasi",
    "The confessors of the Second Iconoclasm": "Wakiri wa Upinzani wa Pili wa Ikoni",
    "The confessors of the iconoclast persecution": "Wakiri wa mateso ya wapinga-ikoni",
    "The countless host of the Soviet-era martyrs, patriarch and peasants, bishops and mothers, gathered around the royal passion-bearers beneath the church they died for.": "Jeshi lisilohesabika la mashahidi wa zama za Kisovieti, patriaki na wakulima, maaskofu na akina mama, wamekusanyika kuzunguka wabeba-mateso wa kifalme chini ya kanisa walilokufa kwa ajili yake.",
    "The deacon Cyriacus and their many companions, martyred with them at Rome": "Shemasi Kiriako na wenzao wengi, walioteswa pamoja nao huko Roma",
    "The deaconess Maria, who buried him": "Shemasi wa kike Maria, aliyemzika",
    "The early Fathers and confessors of Asia Minor": "Mababa wa kwanza na wakiri wa Asia Ndogo",
    "The early Popes and Martyrs of Rome": "Mapapa wa kwanza na Mashahidi wa Roma",
    "The elders Nicephorus and Acacius of the Forerunner Skete": "Wazee Nikeforo na Akakio wa Sketi ya Mtangulizi",
    "The elders Nicephorus and Acacius of the Forerunner Skete, who prepared all three": "Wazee Nikeforo na Akakio wa Sketi ya Mtangulizi, waliowaandaa wote watatu",
    "The elders of Optina, heirs of his school": "Wazee wa Optina, warithi wa shule yake",
    "The elders of the Paisian renewal, whose lineage formed him": "Wazee wa uamsho wa Paisio, ambao ukoo wao ulimlea",
    "The eleven thousand soldiers martyred in Armenia": "Askari elfu kumi na moja walioteswa katika Armenia",
    "The emperor's daughter gathering the bodies of martyrs by night with five virgins, the furnace receiving her companions, the stream of her lonely baptism shining before her repose.": "Binti wa mfalme akikusanya miili ya mashahidi usiku pamoja na mabikira watano, tanuru ikiwapokea wenzake, kijito cha ubatizo wake wa upweke kikiangaza kabla ya kulala kwake.",
    "The evangelist painting the icon of the Theotokos, or writing his Gospel with the ox beside him.": "Mwinjili akiandika ikoni ya Mzazi-Mungu, au akiandika Injili yake na ng'ombe kando yake.",
    "The evangelist writing his Gospel with the angel-man beside him, a tax collector's booth abandoned behind.": "Mwinjili akiandika Injili yake na malaika mwenye sura ya mtu kando yake, kibanda cha mtoza-ushuru kikiachwa nyuma.",
    "The father of monasticism in Rus' in a patched habit, the prosphora of his boyhood and the Studite rule in his hands, the great church rising behind him and the poor of Kyiv at his table.": "Baba wa utawa katika Rus katika vazi lililotiwa viraka, prosfora ya utoto wake na kanuni ya Studio mikononi mwake, kanisa kubwa likiinuka nyuma yake na maskini wa Kyiv mezani pake.",
    "The father of monks in the desert, demons breaking against his prayer like waves, the words Sell all that you have open before him, the whole monastic tree rooted at his feet.": "Baba wa watawa jangwani, mapepo yakivunjika juu ya sala yake kama mawimbi, maneno Uza vyote ulivyo navyo yakiwa wazi mbele yake, mti wote wa utawa ukiwa na mizizi miguuni pake.",
    "The fathers of Scetis and the Egyptian desert": "Mababa wa Sketi na wa jangwa la Misri",
    "The fathers of Scetis, whose sayings preserve him": "Mababa wa Sketi, ambao misemo yao inamhifadhi",
    "The fathers of the Caves who delivered him, among them Nikon, Isaiah of Rostov, and Agapitus the Healer": "Mababa wa Mapango waliomwokoa, miongoni mwao Nikoni, Isaya wa Rostov na Agapito Mponyaji",
    "The fathers of the Caves, with whom he helped deliver Saint Nikita from delusion": "Mababa wa Mapango, ambao pamoja nao alisaidia kumwokoa Mtakatifu Nikita kutoka udanganyifu",
    "The fathers slain at Mar Saba (March 20 and May 16)": "Mababa waliouawa Mar Saba (Machi 20 na Mei 16)",
    "The first hermit of the Holy Mountain in his cave, clothed in his long hair, the Mother of God who chose Athos for her garden above him, fifty-three years of solitude in the wilderness of the sea.": "Mtawa wa kwanza wa upweke wa Mlima Mtakatifu katika pango lake, amevaa nywele zake ndefu, Mzazi-Mungu aliyechagua Athos kuwa bustani yake juu yake, miaka hamsini na mitatu ya upweke katika jangwa la bahari.",
    "The first high priest in his vestments, the budded almond rod in one hand, the censer standing between the dead and the living in the other.": "Kuhani mkuu wa kwanza katika mavazi yake, fimbo ya mlozi iliyochipuka mkono mmoja, chetezo kikisimama kati ya wafu na walio hai mkono mwingine.",
    "The first preachers of the faith in Gaul crowned with martyrdom, the young Church of Périgueux gathered from their labors, the Gospel carried to the western tribes.": "Wahubiri wa kwanza wa imani katika Gali wakivikwa taji ya shahidi, Kanisa changa la Périgueux likikusanywa kutoka kazi zao, Injili ikichukuliwa hadi makabila ya magharibi.",
    "The fisherman of Galilee whom the Lord named the rock, the keys of the Kingdom in his hand, weeping for his denial, crucified head downward at Rome for his Lord.": "Mvuvi wa Galilaya ambaye Bwana alimwita mwamba, funguo za Ufalme mkononi mwake, akililia kukana kwake, akisulubiwa kichwa chini huko Roma kwa ajili ya Bwana wake.",
    "The forty martyrs beheaded with him": "Mashahidi arobaini waliokatwa vichwa pamoja naye",
    "The founder of the common life with the tablet of his rule, the monasteries of Tabennisi filling the Nile island behind him, the angel who gave him the pattern of the cenobium at his side.": "Mwanzilishi wa maisha ya pamoja akiwa na kibao cha kanuni yake, monasteri za Tabenisi zikijaza kisiwa cha Nile nyuma yake, malaika aliyempa mfano wa monasteri ya pamoja kando yake.",
    "The founders and hermits of the Russian forests": "Waanzilishi na watawa wa upweke wa misitu ya Urusi",
    "The founders and hermits of the northern Russian forests": "Waanzilishi na watawa wa upweke wa misitu ya kaskazini ya Urusi",
    "The founders and monastic saints of the Russian north": "Waanzilishi na watakatifu wa kitawa wa kaskazini ya Urusi",
    "The grave of the recluse-bishop opened after four and a half centuries, the body incorrupt as one sleeping, the faithful of Novgorod bringing their blind and dim-eyed to the revealed wonderworker.": "Kaburi la askofu aliyejitenga likifunguliwa baada ya karne nne na nusu, mwili haujaoza kama aliyelala, waamini wa Novgorod wakiwaleta vipofu na wenye macho hafifu kwa mtenda-miujiza aliyefunuliwa.",
})

TEXT.update({
    "The great Emperor and his mother holding between them the Cross she found at Jerusalem, the vision in the sky above and the New Rome he founded below, the liberty of the Church shining from their reign.": "Mfalme mkuu na mama yake wakishika kati yao Msalaba aliouona huko Yerusalemu, maono angani juu na Roma Mpya aliyoijenga chini, uhuru wa Kanisa ukiangaza kutoka utawala wao.",
    "The great Emperor consecrating his new city to the Theotokos, the walls of New Rome rising under the sign of the Cross, Byzantium renamed for its founder and dedicated to God.": "Mfalme mkuu akiuweka wakfu mji wake mpya kwa Mzazi-Mungu, kuta za Roma Mpya zikiinuka chini ya ishara ya Msalaba, Byzantium ikipewa jina la mwanzilishi wake na kuwekwa wakfu kwa Mungu.",
    "The great company of the saints of Rostov and Yaroslavl gathered in ranks, bishops and princes, monks and holy fools, the enlighteners and wonderworkers of a whole region rejoicing together before the Lord.": "Kundi kubwa la watakatifu wa Rostov na Yaroslavl wamekusanyika katika safu, maaskofu na wakuu, watawa na wapumbavu watakatifu, waangazaji na watenda-miujiza wa eneo lote wakishangilia pamoja mbele za Bwana.",
    "The great elder of the Judean desert before his lavra, Sabbas and Cyriacus as youths at his feet, the empress Eudocia receiving his counsel, the Saracen tents turning toward baptism.": "Mzee mkuu wa jangwa la Yudea mbele ya lavra yake, Sabba na Kiriako wakiwa vijana miguuni pake, malkia Eudokia akipokea shauri lake, mahema ya Wasarakeni yakigeukia ubatizo.",
    "The head and part of the relics were long preserved in a reliquary at the Snetogorsk monastery": "Kichwa na sehemu ya masalia vilihifadhiwa kwa muda mrefu katika sanduku takatifu katika monasteri ya Snetogorsk",
    "The head of Hieron was ransomed by the Christian Chrysanthus": "Kichwa cha Hieroni kilikombolewa na Mkristo Krisantho",
    "The head of the Baptist revealed in an earthen vessel, once on the Mount of Olives and once in the cave of Emesa, monks and hierarchs receiving with trembling what Herodias tried to hide.": "Kichwa cha Mbatizaji kikifunuliwa katika chombo cha udongo, mara moja katika Mlima wa Mizeituni na mara moja katika pango la Emesa, watawa na maaskofu wakipokea kwa kutetemeka kile Herodia alichojaribu kukificha.",
    "The hierarchs of Kazan standing together in vestments, the city and its churches beneath them.": "Maaskofu wa Kazan wakisimama pamoja katika mavazi ya ibada, mji na makanisa yake chini yao.",
    "The hierarchs of the Kyivan Church": "Maaskofu wa Kanisa la Kyiv",
    "The holy Bishop of Zahumlje in the mountains of Montenegro, the Prologue's older listing and the historical record naming one and the same wonderworker of Ostrog.": "Askofu mtakatifu wa Zahumlje katika milima ya Montenegro, orodha ya zamani ya Prologo na kumbukumbu ya historia zikimtaja mtenda-miujiza mmoja yuleyule wa Ostrog.",
    "The holy Metropolitans and Patriarchs of Moscow standing in a row in white klobuks and sakkoi, the Dormition cathedral behind.": "Metropolita na Mapatriaki watakatifu wa Moscow wakisimama katika safu wakiwa na klobuku nyeupe na sakosi, kanisa kuu la Kulala nyuma.",
    "The holy Serbian martyrs of the Battle of Kosovo": "Mashahidi watakatifu wa Serbia wa Vita vya Kosovo",
    "The holy ascetics of the Serbian lands": "Watawa watakatifu wa nchi za Serbia",
    "The holy couples and families of the Church": "Wanandoa na familia takatifu za Kanisa",
    "The holy kings and martyrs of the Georgian land": "Wafalme watakatifu na mashahidi wa nchi ya Georgia",
    "The holy martyrs and defenders of the Georgian land": "Mashahidi watakatifu na watetezi wa nchi ya Georgia",
    "The honorable head of the Forerunner recovered from its hiding place at Comana, borne in a silver vessel to Constantinople, the third finding of the Baptist's holy relic.": "Kichwa cha heshima cha Mtangulizi kilichopatikana mahali kilipofichwa huko Komana, kikibebwa katika chombo cha fedha hadi Konstantinopoli, kupatikana kwa tatu kwa masalia matakatifu ya Mbatizaji.",
    "The honorable head of the Forerunner, found a third time at Comana, was carried to Constantinople and enshrined there": "Kichwa cha heshima cha Mtangulizi, kilichopatikana mara ya tatu huko Komana, kilichukuliwa hadi Konstantinopoli na kuwekwa humo",
    "The hospitality of Abraham: three angels at the table beneath the oak of Mamre, Abraham and Sarah serving.": "Ukarimu wa Abrahamu: malaika watatu mezani chini ya mwaloni wa Mamre, Abrahamu na Sara wakihudumu.",
    "The household of the epistle crowned together, Philemon and Apphia at the door of their house church, Archippus the young soldier of Christ between them, the stones of Colossae become their diadems.": "Watu wa nyumba ya waraka wakivikwa taji pamoja, Filemoni na Apfia mlangoni pa kanisa la nyumbani mwao, Arkipo askari kijana wa Kristo kati yao, mawe ya Kolosai yakawa taji zao.",
    "The icon is kept today at Lutsk in Volhynia": "Ikoni yahifadhiwa leo Lutsk katika Volinia",
    "The icon now accompanies the Russian Church Abroad, at the Synodal Cathedral in New York": "Ikoni sasa yaandamana na Kanisa la Urusi Nje ya Nchi, katika Kanisa Kuu la Sinodi huko New York",
    "The image of Christ of the Chalke Gate, which she died to defend": "Sura ya Kristo ya Lango la Halkeia, ambayo alikufa kuitetea",
    "The image was kept at Constantinople (later lost)": "Sura ilihifadhiwa Konstantinopoli (baadaye ilipotea)",
    "The incorrupt patriarch borne back into Constantinople by Methodius and the empress Theodora, entering the City on the very day of his old expulsion, the Holy Apostles receiving him.": "Patriaki asiyeoza akirudishwa Konstantinopoli na Methodio na malkia Theodora, akiingia Mjini siku ileile ya kufukuzwa kwake zamani, Mitume Watakatifu wakimpokea.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the Metropolitan of Moscow revealed amid the fallen stones of his own Chudov monastery, the wonderworker of all Russia found whole after fifty years.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya Metropolita wa Moscow yakifunuliwa kati ya mawe yaliyoanguka ya monasteri yake mwenyewe ya Chudov, mtenda-miujiza wa Urusi yote akipatikana mzima baada ya miaka hamsini.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the abbot Sergius in a shrine; or Sergius as an aged monk in the schema, blessing.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya abate Sergio katika sanduku takatifu; au Sergio kama mtawa mzee katika shahada ya utawa, akibariki.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the boy prince borne from Uglich to Moscow, enshrined in the Kremlin cathedral, the impostors who claimed his name confounded by his body.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya mkuu kijana yakibebwa kutoka Uglich hadi Moscow, yakiwekwa katika kanisa kuu la Kremlin, wajidaio waliolichukua jina lake wakiaibishwa na mwili wake.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the fathers rest in the Near and Far Caves of the Lavra": "Masalia yasiyooza ya mababa yapumzika katika Mapango ya Karibu na ya Mbali ya Lavra",
    "The incorrupt relics of the first archbishop of Kazan borne in solemn translation, the enlightener of the conquered khanate honored by the Church he had planted.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya askofu mkuu wa kwanza wa Kazan yakibebwa katika kuhamishwa kwa sherehe, mwangazaji wa ukhani ulioshindwa akiheshimiwa na Kanisa alilolipanda.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the first bishop of Irkutsk uncovered in the Siberian winter, pilgrims of the whole east streaming to the Ascension monastery.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya askofu wa kwanza wa Irkutsk yakigunduliwa katika baridi ya Siberia, mahujaji wa mashariki yote wakimiminika katika monasteri ya Kupaa.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the founder of Kalyazin uncovered on the bank of the Volga, the Trinity monastery he raised rising behind, the wonderworker given back to his people.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya mwanzilishi wa Kalyazin yakigunduliwa ukingoni mwa Volga, monasteri ya Utatu aliyoijenga ikiinuka nyuma, mtenda-miujiza akirudishwa kwa watu wake.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the great abbot borne in procession to the Studios, the patriarch Methodius at their head, the icons restored shining over the city.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya abate mkuu yakibebwa katika maandamano hadi Studio, patriaki Methodio mbele yao, ikoni zilizorudishwa zikiangaza juu ya mji.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the poor monk of Lukhov found and enshrined, the soldier who became a monk glorified by God with wonders.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya mtawa maskini wa Lukhov yakipatikana na kuwekwa, askari aliyekuwa mtawa akitukuzwa na Mungu kwa miujiza.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the second archbishop of Kazan borne in solemn translation, the founder of Sviyazhsk honored by the Church he had served.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya askofu mkuu wa pili wa Kazan yakibebwa katika kuhamishwa kwa sherehe, mwanzilishi wa Sviyazhsk akiheshimiwa na Kanisa alilolitumikia.",
    "The incorrupt relics of the two princes of Yaroslavl revealed after the fire, the brothers who defended their city against the Tatar honored together, wonders flowing from their shrine.": "Masalia yasiyooza ya wakuu wawili wa Yaroslavl yakifunuliwa baada ya moto, ndugu waliolitetea jiji lao dhidi ya Mtatari wakiheshimiwa pamoja, miujiza ikitiririka kutoka sanduku lao takatifu.",
    "The individual feasts of each of the Twelve throughout the year": "Sikukuu za pekee za kila mmoja wa wale Kumi na Wawili katika mwaka wote",
    "The last prophet with his scroll, the sun of righteousness rising behind him, the messenger's road prepared before the Lord.": "Nabii wa mwisho na gombo lake, jua la haki likichomoza nyuma yake, njia ya mjumbe ikitayarishwa mbele za Bwana.",
    "The later martyrs of Kazan, whose way he opened": "Mashahidi wa baadaye wa Kazan, ambao aliwafungulia njia",
    "The man of God crying against the altar of Bethel as it splits, the king's withered hand outstretched, and on the road home the lion standing sentinel over the prophet it was sent to slay.": "Mtu wa Mungu akiipazia sauti madhabahu ya Betheli ikipasuka, mkono uliopooza wa mfalme ukiwa umenyoshwa, na katika njia ya kurudi simba akisimama mlinzi juu ya nabii aliyetumwa kumwua.",
})

TEXT.update({
    "The many who confessed Christ with them": "Wengi waliomkiri Kristo pamoja nao",
    "The martyred clergy and faithful of the Prague cathedral": "Makasisi na waamini walioteswa wa kanisa kuu la Prague",
    "The martyred dignitaries Bassus, Eusebius, Eutychius, and Basilides, their masters (January 5)": "Watukufu walioteswa Baso, Eusebio, Eutikio na Basilide, mabwana wao (Januari 5)",
    "The martyrs and confessors of the last great persecution": "Mashahidi na wakiri wa mateso makuu ya mwisho",
    "The martyrs and confessors under Julian the Apostate": "Mashahidi na wakiri chini ya Yuliano Mwasi",
    "The martyrs and confessors who suffered with him (commemorated this day)": "Mashahidi na wakiri walioteswa pamoja naye (wanakumbukwa siku hii)",
    "The martyrs and saints of the ancient British Church": "Mashahidi na watakatifu wa Kanisa la kale la Uingereza",
    "The martyrs of Byzantium in the age of the persecutions": "Mashahidi wa Byzantium katika zama za mateso",
    "The martyrs of Comana in Cappadocia": "Mashahidi wa Komana katika Kapadokia",
    "The martyrs of Nicomedia who suffered with him": "Mashahidi wa Nikomedia walioteswa pamoja naye",
    "The martyrs of Persia under Shapur II": "Mashahidi wa Persia chini ya Shapuri wa Pili",
    "The martyrs of the Decian persecution": "Mashahidi wa mateso ya Dekio",
    "The martyrs of the Diocletian persecution": "Mashahidi wa mateso ya Diokletiano",
    "The martyrs of the Persian persecutions": "Mashahidi wa mateso ya Waajemi",
    "The martyrs of the age of the emperors": "Mashahidi wa zama za wafalme",
    "The miracle of her relics at the Fourth Ecumenical Council (July 11)": "Muujiza wa masalia yake katika Mtaguso wa Nne wa Ulimwengu (Julai 11)",
    "The missionary saints of the early Western Church": "Watakatifu wamisionari wa Kanisa la kwanza la Magharibi",
    "The monastery church of Kvabtakhevi filled with monastics and faithful as the flames rise, the hymns ascending with the smoke, Tamerlane's host powerless over the crowned.": "Kanisa la monasteri ya Kvabtakhevi likijaa watawa na waamini miali inapopanda, nyimbo zikipanda pamoja na moshi, jeshi la Tamerlani likiwa halina nguvu juu ya waliovikwa taji.",
    "The mosaic Unbreakable Wall Icon stands in the apse of the Cathedral of Holy Wisdom in Kyiv, preserved intact for nearly a thousand years": "Ikoni ya musa ya Ukuta Usiovunjika yasimama katika kuba ya Kanisa Kuu la Hekima Takatifu huko Kyiv, ikihifadhiwa nzima kwa karibu miaka elfu moja",
    "The mother of the Maccabees, her Old Testament figure": "Mama wa Wamakabayo, sura yake ya Agano la Kale",
    "The multitude of the Persian martyrs of the fourth century": "Umati wa mashahidi wa Persia wa karne ya nne",
    "The myrrh-streaming relics of Saint Nicholas rest at Bari in the basilica raised for them, the holy myrrh continuing to this day": "Masalia ya Mtakatifu Nikolao yatoayo manukato yapumzika Bari katika kanisa kuu lililojengwa kwa ajili yao, manukato matakatifu yakiendelea hata leo",
    "The new martyrs of Mount Athos": "Mashahidi wapya wa Mlima Athos",
    "The new martyrs of the Ottoman yoke": "Mashahidi wapya wa nira ya Waothmani",
    "The new martyrs under the Ottoman yoke": "Mashahidi wapya chini ya nira ya Waothmani",
    "The newborn Virgin cradled by Saint Anna, Joachim beside them, maidens bringing gifts.": "Bikira aliyezaliwa akibembelezwa na Mtakatifu Anna, Yoakimu kando yao, wasichana wakileta zawadi.",
    "The ninety sisters of her convent": "Dada tisini wa monasteri yake ya wanawake",
    "The one hundred and fifty Fathers gathered at Constantinople with the completed Creed before them, the divinity of the Holy Spirit confessed, the heresy of Macedonius cast down.": "Mababa mia moja na hamsini waliokusanyika Konstantinopoli na Kanuni ya Imani iliyokamilika mbele yao, Umungu wa Roho Mtakatifu ukikiriwa, uzushi wa Makedonio ukiangushwa.",
    "The passion-bearers Boris and Gleb, the first of the Rus' princely martyrs (July 24)": "Wabeba-mateso Boris na Gleb, wa kwanza wa wakuu mashahidi wa Rus (Julai 24)",
    "The patriarch and clergy placing the Lord's Robe within a reliquary in the Dormition Cathedral.": "Patriaki na makasisi wakiweka Vazi la Bwana ndani ya sanduku takatifu katika Kanisa Kuu la Kulala.",
    "The patriarch and clergy placing the Virgin's robe within a reliquary at Blachernae, the Mother of God enthroned above.": "Patriaki na makasisi wakiweka vazi la Bikira ndani ya sanduku takatifu huko Blakerne, Mzazi-Mungu ameketi juu.",
    "The people of Constantinople standing the whole night through singing to the Mother of God, the enemy fleets broken on the walls she guards, the unseated hymn of the unseated City.": "Watu wa Konstantinopoli wakisimama usiku kucha wakimwimbia Mzazi-Mungu, majeshi ya meli ya adui yakivunjika kwenye kuta anazozilinda, wimbo usioketi wa Mji usioketi.",
    "The pillar of Orthodoxy at rest at last on his throne of Alexandria, the five exiles behind him like waves that failed, the Creed he defended shining in his hand.": "Nguzo ya Othodoksi akipumzika mwishowe katika kiti chake cha Aleksandria, uhamisho mara tano nyuma yake kama mawimbi yaliyoshindwa, Kanuni ya Imani aliyoitetea ikiangaza mkononi mwake.",
    "The precious Cross adorned and prepared for exaltation.": "Msalaba wa thamani ukipambwa na kuandaliwa kwa kuinuliwa.",
    "The precious Cross enthroned on flowers in the midst of the church, the faithful of mid-Lent bowing before it, the Resurrection shining through it from three weeks away.": "Msalaba wa thamani umewekwa juu ya maua katikati ya kanisa, waamini wa katikati ya Kwaresima wakiuinamia, Ufufuo ukiangaza kupitia huo kutoka majuma matatu mbele.",
    "The precious Cross exalted upon the ambo, venerated by the faithful.": "Msalaba wa thamani ukiinuliwa juu ya ambo, ukiheshimiwa na waamini.",
    "The precious Cross venerated a final time before its return to the sanctuary.": "Msalaba wa thamani ukiheshimiwa kwa mara ya mwisho kabla ya kurudishwa patakatifu.",
    "The precious head of the Forerunner, found on the Mount of Olives and again at Emesa in 452": "Kichwa cha thamani cha Mtangulizi, kilichopatikana katika Mlima wa Mizeituni na tena huko Emesa mwaka 452",
    "The presbyter Acacius, who baptized him": "Kasisi Akakio, aliyembatiza",
    "The priest with the spear of his zeal, the plague halted at his act, the covenant of an everlasting priesthood descending upon him.": "Kuhani mwenye mkuki wa bidii yake, pigo likizuiliwa kwa tendo lake, agano la ukuhani wa milele likimshukia.",
})

TEXT.update({
    "The priests Eugenius and Macarius, for whom he interceded": "Makasisi Eugenio na Makario, ambao aliwaombea",
    "The principal feast of Saint Theodore and his sons (September 19)": "Sikukuu kuu ya Mtakatifu Theodoro na wanawe (Septemba 19)",
    "The principal feast of the Pochaev Icon (July 23)": "Sikukuu kuu ya Ikoni ya Pochaev (Julai 23)",
    "The prophet before the throne high and lifted up, the seraph's coal touching his lips, the scroll of Immanuel and of the Servant wounded for our transgressions unrolling toward Bethlehem and Golgotha.": "Nabii mbele ya kiti cha enzi kilicho juu na kilichoinuliwa, kaa la serafi likigusa midomo yake, gombo la Imanueli na la Mtumishi aliyejeruhiwa kwa makosa yetu likikunjuka kuelekea Bethlehemu na Golgotha.",
    "The prophet borne by an angel over Babylon, bringing food to Daniel in the lions' den.": "Nabii akibebwa na malaika juu ya Babeli, akimletea Danieli chakula katika tundu la simba.",
    "The prophet in the lions' den, the Ancient of Days and one like the Son of Man in the heavens above him.": "Nabii katika tundu la simba, Mzee wa Siku na mmoja aliye kama Mwana wa Adamu katika mbingu juu yake.",
    "The pyre of Vracar with the reliquary of Sava upon it, the smoke ascending like incense over the Serbian land, the great white temple rising from the ashes of the hill.": "Moto wa Vracar ukiwa na sanduku takatifu la Sava juu yake, moshi ukipanda kama ubani juu ya nchi ya Serbia, hekalu kubwa jeupe likiinuka kutoka majivu ya kilima.",
    "The ranks of Novgorod's bishops and archbishops gathered in their own cathedral, Holy Wisdom rising over the succession of a thousand years.": "Safu za maaskofu na maaskofu wakuu wa Novgorod wamekusanyika katika kanisa lao kuu, Hekima Takatifu ikiinuka juu ya urithi wa miaka elfu moja.",
    "The ranks of the new martyrs of Butovo, bishops and priests and simple believers, gathered in glory above the grave pits where they were shot, the Russian Golgotha crowned with saints.": "Safu za mashahidi wapya wa Butovo, maaskofu na makasisi na waamini wa kawaida, wamekusanyika katika utukufu juu ya mashimo ya makaburi walipopigwa risasi, Golgotha ya Urusi ikivikwa taji ya watakatifu.",
    "The relics of Constantine and his sons Michael and Theodore rest at Murom, in the church of the Annunciation they founded": "Masalia ya Konstantino na wanawe Mikaeli na Theodoro yapumzika Murom, katika kanisa la Bishara walilolianzisha",
    "The relics of Saint Eugene were enshrined at Trebizond, whose patron he became": "Masalia ya Mtakatifu Eugenio yaliwekwa Trapezunt, ambao akawa mlinzi wao",
    "The relics of Saint Sava were burned at Vracar in 1594; the great church of Saint Sava now stands upon the place": "Masalia ya Mtakatifu Sava yaliteketezwa Vracar mwaka 1594; kanisa kubwa la Mtakatifu Sava sasa lasimama mahali pale",
    "The relics of the Egyptian martyr borne into Constantinople, the woman's blinded eye healed by a drop of his blood at the place of his torment.": "Masalia ya shahidi Mmisri yakiingizwa Konstantinopoli, jicho la mwanamke lililopofuka likiponywa kwa tone la damu yake mahali pa mateso yake.",
    "The relics of the Rostov and Yaroslavl saints rest in the churches and monasteries of their region, a treasury of the land's holiness": "Masalia ya watakatifu wa Rostov na Yaroslavl yapumzika katika makanisa na monasteri za eneo lao, hazina ya utakatifu wa nchi",
    "The relics of the apostles are honored throughout the Church they founded in every land": "Masalia ya mitume yaheshimiwa katika Kanisa lote walilolianzisha katika kila nchi",
    "The relics of the archbishop borne in procession to the Yuriev monastery, the sick healed along the way, the chapel of Photius receiving them.": "Masalia ya askofu mkuu yakibebwa katika maandamano hadi monasteri ya Yuriev, wagonjwa wakiponywa njiani, kanisa dogo la Fotio likiyapokea.",
    "The relics of the general-martyr Theodore borne home to Euchaita, the soldier-saint honored in his own city, the crowds of pilgrims gathered to his shrine.": "Masalia ya Theodoro shahidi jemadari yakibebwa nyumbani hadi Eukaita, mtakatifu askari akiheshimiwa katika mji wake mwenyewe, makundi ya mahujaji yakikusanyika kwenye sanduku lake takatifu.",
    "The relics of the holy prince borne on Pascha morning to their new shrine in the Trinity cathedral he built, his sword with its Latin device beside him, Pskov keeping its protector.": "Masalia ya mkuu mtakatifu yakibebwa asubuhi ya Pasaka hadi sanduku lao jipya katika kanisa kuu la Utatu alilolijenga, upanga wake wenye andiko la Kilatini kando yake, Pskov ikimhifadhi mlinzi wake.",
    "The relics of the two passion-bearers borne on the shoulders of princes into the new church of Vyshhorod, the feuding house of Rus' momentarily one procession behind its two meekest sons.": "Masalia ya wabeba-mateso wawili yakibebwa mabegani mwa wakuu hadi kanisa jipya la Vyshhorod, nyumba ya Rus iliyokuwa na ugomvi ikiwa kwa muda maandamano moja nyuma ya wanawe wapole kuliko wote.",
    "The relics of the unmercenary martyrs Cyrus and John borne in translation to Menuthis, the shrine of the demons cast down, the sick healed at the fountain of the saints.": "Masalia ya mashahidi wasiopokea-malipo Kiro na Yohane yakibebwa katika kuhamishwa hadi Menuthi, mahali patakatifu pa mapepo pakiangushwa, wagonjwa wakiponywa kwenye chemchemi ya watakatifu.",
    "The right-believing princes of the Kyivan and Novgorod lands": "Wakuu waaminifu wa nchi za Kyiv na Novgorod",
    "The righteous Anna, an elderly matron in a maphorion, holding the infant Mary, or reposing with saints attending.": "Mwenye haki Anna, mama mzee katika maforio, akimshika Maria mchanga, au akilala huku watakatifu wakihudumu.",
    "The righteous man on the ash heap with the potsherd, the four messengers of ruin behind him and the whirlwind of the Answer before him, the doubled flocks and the new children shining at the edge of the trial.": "Mtu mwenye haki juu ya lundo la majivu akiwa na kigae, wajumbe wanne wa maangamizi nyuma yake na kimbunga cha Jibu mbele yake, makundi yaliyoongezwa maradufu na watoto wapya wakiangaza ukingoni mwa jaribu.",
    "The righteous of the Old Testament": "Wenye haki wa Agano la Kale",
    "The righteous youths and child-saints of the Russian land": "Vijana wenye haki na watoto watakatifu wa nchi ya Urusi",
    "The rock bearing the imprint of the Theotokos' foot, and the spring that fills it, are enshrined at the Dormition Lavra of Pochaiv, a fountain of healings to this day": "Mwamba wenye alama ya mguu wa Mzazi-Mungu, na chemchemi ikiujaza, vimewekwa katika Lavra ya Kulala ya Pochaiv, chemchemi ya uponyaji hata leo",
    "The ruler of the Corinthian synagogue beaten before the judgment seat of Gallio, then standing beside Paul as the epistle opens with his name, the church of Colophon at his blessing.": "Mkuu wa sinagogi la Korintho akipigwa mbele ya kiti cha hukumu cha Galio, kisha akisimama kando ya Paulo waraka unapofunguka kwa jina lake, kanisa la Kolofoni likiwa chini ya baraka yake.",
    "The sailors of Bari bearing the relics of Nicholas from the myrrh-filled tomb of Myra to their ships, the wonderworker arriving in the West with his myrrh unbroken, the churches of Rus' keeping the spring feast with love.": "Mabaharia wa Bari wakibeba masalia ya Nikolao kutoka kaburi lililojaa manukato la Mira hadi meli zao, mtenda-miujiza akiwasili Magharibi na manukato yake bila kukatika, makanisa ya Rus yakiadhimisha sikukuu ya majira ya kuchipua kwa upendo.",
    "The saints and enlighteners of the Russian north": "Watakatifu na waangazaji wa kaskazini ya Urusi",
    "The saints of Volhynia gathered about the Pochaiv icon of the Mother of God, the Lavra on its hill behind.": "Watakatifu wa Volinia wamekusanyika kuzunguka ikoni ya Pochaiv ya Mzazi-Mungu, Lavra juu ya kilima chake nyuma.",
    "The saints of the Dionysiou monastery": "Watakatifu wa monasteri ya Dionisiu",
    "The scorched church of Kvabtakhevi itself has stood as their reliquary and memorial": "Kanisa lililoungua la Kvabtakhevi lenyewe limesimama kama sanduku lao takatifu na ukumbusho wao",
    "The sea gave back their bodies, which the faithful of Thessalonica buried with honor": "Bahari ilirudisha miili yao, ambayo waamini wa Thessalonica waliizika kwa heshima",
    "The sea, shaken by an earthquake, cast the body of Apphianus back before the gates of Caesarea": "Bahari, iliyotikiswa na tetemeko, ilirudisha mwili wa Apfiano mbele ya malango ya Kaisaria",
    "The second son of Jacob by Leah, one of the twelve patriarchs": "Mwana wa pili wa Yakobo kwa Lea, mmoja wa mababu kumi na wawili",
    "The seven Maccabee brothers, her sons": "Ndugu saba Wamakabayo, wanawe",
    "The seven Maccabee brothers, his disciples": "Ndugu saba Wamakabayo, wanafunzi wake",
    "The seven Virgin Martyrs of Ancyra whom he buried (May 18)": "Mabikira Mashahidi saba wa Ancyra aliowazika (Mei 18)",
    "The six brethren martyred with him": "Ndugu sita walioteswa pamoja naye",
    "The soldier-martyrs of the age of the emperors": "Askari mashahidi wa zama za wafalme",
})

TEXT.update({
    "The soldier-martyrs of the early Church": "Askari mashahidi wa Kanisa la kwanza",
    "The star withdrawing above the cave, the Church singing the festal hymns once more in fullness before the door of the feast is closed.": "Nyota ikijiondoa juu ya pango, Kanisa likiimba nyimbo za sikukuu tena kwa ukamilifu kabla mlango wa sikukuu haujafungwa.",
    "The stylites and dendrites of the Christian East": "Watawa wa nguzo na wa miti wa Mashariki ya Kikristo",
    "The three hundred and eighteen God-bearing Fathers gathered at Nicaea, the scroll of the Creed before them, Arius cast down beneath their feet, the divinity of the Son confessed.": "Mababa mia tatu na kumi na wanane wabeba-Mungu waliokusanyika Nicea, gombo la Kanuni ya Imani mbele yao, Ario akiangushwa chini ya miguu yao, Umungu wa Mwana ukikiriwa.",
    "The tomb of the Great Martyr George at Lydda": "Kaburi la Shahidi Mkuu Georgi huko Lida",
    "The tradition of the West tells of his relics honored in Spain, at Compostela, from ancient times": "Mapokeo ya Magharibi yasema masalia yake yaliheshimiwa katika Hispania, huko Compostela, tangu zamani",
    "The translation of his relics (August 14)": "Kuhamishwa kwa masalia yake (Agosti 14)",
    "The translation of his relics (August 30)": "Kuhamishwa kwa masalia yake (Agosti 30)",
    "The translation of his relics, commemorated on August 25": "Kuhamishwa kwa masalia yake, kunakokumbukwa Agosti 25",
    "The translation of their relics to Menuthis (June 28)": "Kuhamishwa kwa masalia yao hadi Menuthi (Juni 28)",
    "The twelve apostles gathered in one assembly, each with the emblem of his preaching and his martyrdom, the foundations of the Church honored together.": "Mitume kumi na wawili wamekusanyika katika kusanyiko moja, kila mmoja akiwa na alama ya mahubiri yake na ya kuuawa kwake, misingi ya Kanisa ikiheshimiwa pamoja.",
    "The twenty-three martyrs of Nicomedia with them": "Mashahidi ishirini na watatu wa Nikomedia pamoja nao",
    "The two Thessalonian brothers holding the scroll of the Slavonic alphabet and the translated Gospel, Moravia at their feet and the whole future of Slavic Orthodoxy in their gift.": "Ndugu wawili wa Thessalonica wakishika gombo la herufi za Kislavoni na Injili iliyotafsiriwa, Moravia miguuni pao na wakati wote ujao wa Othodoksi ya Kislavoni katika zawadi yao.",
    "The two chief apostles embracing, Peter with the keys and Paul with the sword and the scroll, the pillars of the Church crowned together with martyrdom at Rome.": "Mitume wawili wakuu wakikumbatiana, Petro na funguo na Paulo na upanga na gombo, nguzo za Kanisa zikivikwa taji ya shahidi pamoja huko Roma.",
    "The two sisters of Bethany, Martha serving and Mary seated at the feet of the Lord, the tomb of Lazarus behind them from which their brother came forth at Christ's word.": "Dada wawili wa Bethania, Martha akihudumu na Maria ameketi miguuni pa Bwana, kaburi la Lazaro nyuma yao ambamo ndugu yao alitoka kwa neno la Kristo.",
    "The two soldiers who suffered with him": "Askari wawili walioteswa pamoja naye",
    "The uncounted host of Persia's martyrs, their relics borne across the frontier into the city built to hold them.": "Jeshi lisilohesabika la mashahidi wa Persia, masalia yao yakibebwa kuvuka mpaka hadi mji uliojengwa kuyahifadhi.",
    "The uncovering of her relics and her repose, commemorated on October 2": "Kugunduliwa kwa masalia yake na kulala kwake, kunakokumbukwa Oktoba 2",
    "The uncovering of her relics, commemorated on this day": "Kugunduliwa kwa masalia yake, kunakokumbukwa siku hii",
    "The uncovering of his relics (April 17)": "Kugunduliwa kwa masalia yake (Aprili 17)",
    "The uncovering of his relics and glorification (September 9)": "Kugunduliwa kwa masalia yake na kutangazwa kwake mtakatifu (Septemba 9)",
    "The uncovering of the relics in the cave, or the archdeacon Stephen in diaconal vestments holding a censer and a model church.": "Kugunduliwa kwa masalia katika pango, au shemasi mkuu Stefano katika mavazi ya kishemasi akishika chetezo na kielelezo cha kanisa.",
    "The venerable Petka holding a cross and a vessel of healing water, a spring flowing at her feet.": "Mheshimiwa Petka akishika msalaba na chombo cha maji ya uponyaji, chemchemi ikitiririka miguuni pake.",
    "The virgin-martyrs of the Roman persecutions": "Mabikira mashahidi wa mateso ya Kirumi",
    "The virgin-martyrs of the age of the emperors": "Mabikira mashahidi wa zama za wafalme",
    "The weeping prophet over burning Jerusalem, the almond branch and the potter's clay beside him, the scroll of the new covenant written on hearts unrolling from his hand.": "Nabii anayelia juu ya Yerusalemu inayoteketea, tawi la mlozi na udongo wa mfinyanzi kando yake, gombo la agano jipya lililoandikwa mioyoni likikunjuka kutoka mkononi mwake.",
    "The woman of Jacob's well holding the vessel of living water, her sons and sisters around her in martyrs' crowns, Nero's daughter kneeling converted, the well of her last confession beneath her.": "Mwanamke wa kisima cha Yakobo akishika chombo cha maji ya uzima, wanawe na dada zake wakimzunguka katika taji za mashahidi, binti wa Nero akipiga magoti akiwa ameongoka, kisima cha ukiri wake wa mwisho chini yake.",
    "The wonderworking Bogolyubov Icon was enshrined at Bogolyubovo, the residence Saint Andrew built at the place of the Mother of God's appearing": "Ikoni ya Bogolyubov itendayo miujiza iliwekwa Bogolyubovo, makazi ambayo Mtakatifu Andrea aliyajenga mahali pa kutokea kwa Mzazi-Mungu",
    "The wonderworking Glykophilousa icon is enshrined at the Philotheou monastery on Mount Athos, and a spring of holy water marks the shore where it arrived": "Ikoni ya Glikofilusa itendayo miujiza imewekwa katika monasteri ya Filotheu katika Mlima Athos, na chemchemi ya maji matakatifu yaonyesha ufuo ilipowasili",
    "The wonderworking Kasperov Icon was enshrined in the Kherson region and honored at Odessa, which it delivered in the Crimean War": "Ikoni ya Kasperov itendayo miujiza iliwekwa katika eneo la Kherson na kuheshimiwa Odessa, ambayo iliikomboa katika Vita vya Krimea",
    "The wonderworking Kyiv-Bratsk Icon was enshrined at the Brotherhood monastery of the Kyiv Podil, the home of the famous Kyivan school": "Ikoni ya Kyiv-Bratsk itendayo miujiza iliwekwa katika monasteri ya Undugu ya Podil ya Kyiv, makao ya shule maarufu ya Kyiv",
    "The wonderworking Passion Icon was enshrined at Moscow, where a monastery, the Strastnoy, was built in its honor": "Ikoni ya Mateso itendayo miujiza iliwekwa Moscow, ambapo monasteri, Strastnoy, ilijengwa kwa heshima yake",
    "The wonderworking Vladimir Icon, protectress of Russia, is honored on this and other days of the city's deliverances": "Ikoni ya Vladimir itendayo miujiza, mlinzi wa Urusi, yaheshimiwa siku hii na siku nyingine za ukombozi wa mji",
    "The wonderworking Yaroslavl-Pechersk Icon, of the Kiev-Caves type, was glorified in 1823 in the church of the Procession of the Cross under the belltower of the Yaroslavl bishop's residence": "Ikoni ya Yaroslavl-Pechersk itendayo miujiza, ya namna ya Mapango ya Kiev, ilitukuzwa mwaka 1823 katika kanisa la Maandamano ya Msalaba chini ya mnara wa kengele wa makazi ya askofu wa Yaroslavl",
    "The wonderworking and unmercenary saints of the Church": "Watakatifu watenda-miujiza na wasiopokea-malipo wa Kanisa",
    "The wonderworking icon is enshrined at the convent of Kozelshchyna": "Ikoni itendayo miujiza imewekwa katika monasteri ya wanawake ya Kozelshchyna",
    "The wonderworking icon was enshrined in the Dormition cathedral of the Joseph-Volokolamsk monastery": "Ikoni itendayo miujiza iliwekwa katika kanisa kuu la Kulala la monasteri ya Iosifu-Volokolamsk",
    "The wonderworking icon was glorified at the Saint Nicholas monastery of Odrino and in a celebrated copy at Moscow, streaming myrrh and healing many": "Ikoni itendayo miujiza ilitukuzwa katika monasteri ya Mtakatifu Nikolao ya Odrino na katika nakala maarufu huko Moscow, ikitiririka manukato na kuponya wengi",
    "The wonderworking icon was glorified at the Vladychny monastery of Serpukhov, and its grace has continued through its honored copies": "Ikoni itendayo miujiza ilitukuzwa katika monasteri ya Vladychny ya Serpukhov, na neema yake imeendelea kupitia nakala zake zinazoheshimiwa",
    "The wonderworking icon was treasured at the Lubyatov monastery of Saint Nicholas near Pskov": "Ikoni itendayo miujiza ilihifadhiwa katika monasteri ya Lubyatov ya Mtakatifu Nikolao karibu na Pskov",
})

TEXT.update({
    "The wonderworking icon, of the Caves tradition of Venerable Alipy, was enshrined at the Dormition monastery founded on the Svena": "Ikoni itendayo miujiza, ya mapokeo ya Mapango ya Mheshimiwa Alipio, iliwekwa katika monasteri ya Kulala iliyoanzishwa kando ya Svena",
    "The wonderworking icons of the Mother of God": "Ikoni za Mzazi-Mungu zitendazo miujiza",
    "The wonderworking icons of the Mother of God of the Kyivan land": "Ikoni za Mzazi-Mungu zitendazo miujiza za nchi ya Kyiv",
    "The wonderworking icons of the Mother of God of the Russian land": "Ikoni za Mzazi-Mungu zitendazo miujiza za nchi ya Urusi",
    "The wonderworking icons of the Mother of God of the southern Russian lands": "Ikoni za Mzazi-Mungu zitendazo miujiza za nchi za kusini za Urusi",
    "The wonderworking “Seven Arrows” Icon was glorified at Vologda, found long neglected upon a belltower stair": "Ikoni ya 'Mishale Saba' itendayo miujiza ilitukuzwa Vologda, ikipatikana ikiwa imesahauliwa kwa muda mrefu juu ya ngazi ya mnara wa kengele",
    "The wonderworking “Surety of Sinners” Icon is enshrined at the Holy Trinity convent of Korets in Volhynia": "Ikoni ya 'Mdhamini wa Wenye Dhambi' itendayo miujiza imewekwa katika monasteri ya wanawake ya Utatu Mtakatifu ya Korets katika Volinia",
    "The young bishop of Ephesus with the epistles addressed to him, Paul's hand on his shoulder, the idol procession he opposed raging behind his crown.": "Askofu kijana wa Efeso akiwa na nyaraka zilizoandikwa kwake, mkono wa Paulo begani mwake, maandamano ya sanamu aliyoyapinga yakivuma nyuma ya taji yake.",
    "The youngest of the twelve patriarchs, Joseph's silver cup beside him, a wolf at morning and evening at his feet.": "Mdogo kuliko mababu kumi na wawili, kikombe cha fedha cha Yosefu kando yake, mbwa-mwitu asubuhi na jioni miguuni pake.",
    "The youths Urban, Prilidian, and Epolonius, and their mother Christodula": "Vijana Urbano, Prilidiano na Epoloni, na mama yao Kristodula",
    "The “Softening of Evil Hearts” Icon of the same type": "Ikoni ya 'Kulainisha Mioyo Migumu' ya namna ileile",
    "Thebaid, Egypt": "Thebaida, Misri",
    "Thebes": "Thebe",
    "Thebes of Egypt": "Thebe ya Misri",
    "Thebes, Boeotia, Greece": "Thebe, Boiotia, Ugiriki",
    "Thebes, Egypt": "Thebe, Misri",
    "Their brother Saint Lazarus the Four-days-dead (October 17 and Lazarus Saturday)": "Ndugu yao Mtakatifu Lazaro Aliyekaa Siku Nne (Oktoba 17 na Jumamosi ya Lazaro)",
    "Their burial place on the Via Salaria became a shrine of the Roman church": "Mahali pao pa kuzikwa katika Via Salaria pakawa mahali patakatifu pa kanisa la Roma",
    "Their burned remains, cast into the river, were gathered by the faithful; portions spread through all the Church": "Mabaki yao yaliyoteketezwa, yaliyotupwa mtoni, yalikusanywa na waamini; sehemu zilienea katika Kanisa lote",
    "Their commemoration was kept of old at the monastery of Paulopetrion": "Ukumbusho wao uliadhimishwa tangu kale katika monasteri ya Paulopetrio",
    "Their common feast with the Slavic enlightenment (May 11)": "Sikukuu yao ya pamoja na uangazaji wa Waslavoni (Mei 11)",
    "Their heads were venerated in Hagia Sophia at Constantinople, seen by the pilgrim Anthony in 1200": "Vichwa vyao viliheshimiwa katika Hagia Sofia huko Konstantinopoli, vikionwa na mhujaji Antonio mwaka 1200",
    "Their incorrupt relics rest at Menyusha in the Novgorod land, glorified by healings": "Masalia yao yasiyooza yapumzika Menyusha katika nchi ya Novgorod, yakitukuzwa kwa uponyaji",
    "Their incorrupt relics rest at the Holy Spirit monastery in Vilnius; the altar of the church was set upon the base of the oak on which they suffered": "Masalia yao yasiyooza yapumzika katika monasteri ya Roho Mtakatifu huko Vilnius; madhabahu ya kanisa iliwekwa juu ya shina la mwaloni ambao juu yake waliteswa",
    "Their incorrupt relics were discovered at Lentini in 1517, where the three brothers are honored as patrons of the city": "Masalia yao yasiyooza yaligunduliwa Lentini mwaka 1517, ambapo ndugu watatu huheshimiwa kama walinzi wa mji",
    "Their incorrupt relics, uncovered after a fire in 1501, rest at the cathedral of Yaroslavl": "Masalia yao yasiyooza, yaliyogunduliwa baada ya moto mwaka 1501, yapumzika katika kanisa kuu la Yaroslavl",
    "Their martyrdom, commemorated on January 31": "Kuuawa kwao, kunakokumbukwa Januari 31",
    "Their memory and church have been kept at Kerkyra from the earliest ages": "Kumbukumbu yao na kanisa lao vimehifadhiwa Kerkira tangu zama za mwanzo",
    "Their memory is kept also on March 13 with services of old at the Paulopetrion": "Kumbukumbu yao huadhimishwa pia Machi 13 kwa ibada za tangu kale katika Paulopetrio",
    "Their principal commemoration (June 28)": "Ukumbusho wao mkuu (Juni 28)",
    "Their principal commemoration with the larger company is kept on April 10": "Ukumbusho wao mkuu pamoja na kundi kubwa huadhimishwa Aprili 10",
    "Their relics are honored at Rome, where both were martyred under Nero on this day": "Masalia yao yaheshimiwa Roma, ambapo wote wawili waliuawa chini ya Nero siku hii",
    "Their relics rest at Avnezh, where they founded their monastery and were slain": "Masalia yao yapumzika Avnezh, ambapo walianzisha monasteri yao na wakauawa",
    "Their relics rest at the Valaam monastery on Lake Ladoga, which they founded; they were borne to Novgorod for safety and returned": "Masalia yao yapumzika katika monasteri ya Valaam katika Ziwa Ladoga, waliyoianzisha; yalibebwa Novgorod kwa usalama na kurudishwa",
    "Their relics rest together at Murom, in the single tomb they had prepared, glorified as the patrons of Christian marriage": "Masalia yao yapumzika pamoja Murom, katika kaburi moja walilokuwa wamelitayarisha, wakitukuzwa kama walinzi wa ndoa ya Kikristo",
    "Their relics were among those discovered at Constantinople in a place called Eugenius, revealed by divine revelation": "Masalia yao yalikuwa kati ya yale yaliyogunduliwa Konstantinopoli mahali paitwapo Eugenio, yakifunuliwa kwa ufunuo wa Mungu",
    "Their relics were honored at Ancyra, where they suffered": "Masalia yao yaliheshimiwa Ancyra, ambapo waliteswa",
    "Their relics were honored at Ancyra; the place of the virgins' burial, chosen with the priest Fronto, became a shrine": "Masalia yao yaliheshimiwa Ancyra; mahali pa kuzikwa kwa mabikira, palipochaguliwa pamoja na kasisi Fronto, pakawa mahali patakatifu",
    "Their relics were honored at Byzantium, where they suffered": "Masalia yao yaliheshimiwa Byzantium, ambapo waliteswa",
    "Their relics were honored at Byzantium, where they were martyred": "Masalia yao yaliheshimiwa Byzantium, ambapo waliuawa",
})

